    "body": "### Acknowledgements\n\n- [X] I acknowledge that I have read the above items\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nLocalStorage of \"greylisted\" websites is not cleared at browser restart (and maybe also some other piece of data)\r\nI detected the bug in particular with website https://www.lefigaro.fr/\r\n\r\nThe first time you access to this website, it asks for your consent to cookies, and records your answer, in order to do not ask you the same at your next access.\r\nYour consent is not stored in a cookie (lefigaro.fr do not actually create any cookie) but in LocalStorage.\r\n\r\nIf there is no rule defined in CAD relative to this website, cleansing of this data (your consent) is correctlty done by CAD if you close the tab, a/o switch in the tab to another domain a/o restart the browser, and when the cleansing is done, re-opening the site asks again for your consent.\r\n\r\nBut if there is a \"GreyList\" rule defined on the domain, with all boxes checked (\"Keep ... until restart\"), the cleansing is not done if you \"only\" close the tab or switch to another domain (which is expected behaviour), but no cleansing as well is done EVEN IF YOU RESTART browser... whch is a bug.\r\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\nSteps to reproduce \r\n\r\nStep 1:\r\nTo start on a \"blank page\", clear in Firefox all data relative to any website.\r\nDo not create any rule in CAD, neither Blank nor Grey, relative to lefigaro.fr\r\nSuspend automatic cleansing in CAD\r\nOpen www.lefigaro.fr and give (or reject) your consent to cookies\r\nClose the tab, or switch to another domain, or restart the browser\r\nOpen again www.lefigaro.fr and see that your consent is no more asked\r\nActivate automatic cleansing in CAD\r\nClose the tab (the one opend on lefigaro.fr), or switch to another domain, or restart the browser\r\nWait for automatic cleansing\r\nOpen again www.lefigaro.fr and see that now your consent is again asked.\r\n\r\nStep 2 :\r\nTo start also this 2nd step on a \"blank page\", clear again in Firefox all data relative to any website.\r\nCreate in CAD a \"GreyList\" rule, on \"*.lefigaro.fr\", with all boxes (\"keep until restart\") checked.\r\nActivate automatic cleansing in CAD\r\nOpen www.lefigaro.fr and give (or reject) your consent to cookies\r\nClose the tab, or switch to another domain.\r\nOpen again www.lefigaro.fr and verify that your consent is no more asked (normal, since \"GreyList\")\r\nRestart the browser\r\nWait for automatic cleansing\r\nOpen again www.lefigaro.fr and see that your consent is still no more asked.... while it should if cleansing at restart has been effective.\r\n\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nTo have ALL data relative to GreyListed website (including the LocaStorage) cleared at browser restart,and then to have the website asking again for your consent to cookies.\n\n### Screenshots\n\n_No response_\n\n### System Info - Operating System (OS)\n\nWindows 10 Pro 21H1\n\n### System Info - Browser Info\n\nFirefox 90.0.2 (64 bits)\n\n### System Info - CookieAutoDelete Version\n\n3.6.0\n\n### Additional Context\n\n_No response_",
